    <string name="help_title">Help</string>
    <string name="help_message">TOOLS\n- Select: pick bones, slots and shapes.\n- Bone: add a root or child bone.\n- Shape: add a rectangle, ellipse or triangle.\n- Move, Rotate, Scale: transform the selection.\n- Pan: move the canvas.\n\nANIMATION\n- Create an animation and select it in the timeline.\n- Move the playhead, change bones, then press Key.\n- Play and Stop preview the animation. Loop toggles looping.\n- Switch skins with the Skin button. Skin key stores a skin change at the playhead time (saved only in .spineproj).\n\nIMAGES AND EXPORT\n- Import PNG or JPG as an attachment.\n- Export Spine JSON or ZIP. The ZIP contains skeleton.json, atlas.atlas and atlas.png. Unpack it and import into Spine Desktop.\n- .spineproj is the internal mobile format. It keeps skin keys and procedural shapes. Spine JSON export uses standard fields only.\n\nLIMITATIONS\n- Meshes, IK, transform/path/physics constraints and other advanced Spine features are not edited in the mobile version yet.</string>
    <string name="about_title">About</string>
    <string name="about_message">Spine Editor Mobile\nVersion %1$s\n\nA mobile-first editor for 2D bone animation. Create bones, slots, procedural shapes and image attachments, animate them on the timeline, switch skins and export to Spine.\n\nCreated by MergeGames and the imaginary Bandjou.\n\nSupported: bones, slots, region and image attachments, procedural shapes, skins, skin keys, bone animation, draw order, events, PNG export, Spine JSON and ZIP export.\n\nNot supported yet: meshes, IK, transform/path/physics constraints, clipping, blend modes and other advanced Spine features.</string>
